==============================================================================
WRITE OPERATIONS AND MACHINE STATE
==============================================================================

The Software provides write operations that CHANGE THE STATE of connected
equipment (for example, writing PLC/PMC memory, tool or work offsets,
variables, or part-program files). The Software does not itself provide
high-level machine-control functions such as cycle start or cycle stop.
However, write operations, including PLC/PMC memory writes, may be used to
influence equipment behavior; this capability is provided by the equipment's
own vendor interfaces and may be exercised through them independently of the
Software.

You are solely responsible for determining whether any write operation is
safe in your environment and for all consequences of performing it. TO THE
MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE AUTHOR ACCEPTS NO
RESPONSIBILITY OR LIABILITY, AND SHALL OWE NO COMPENSATION OF ANY KIND, FOR
ANY DAMAGE, LOSS, INJURY, OR OTHER HARM ARISING FROM ANY WRITE OPERATION OR
ANY RESULTING CHANGE TO EQUIPMENT STATE, HOWEVER CAUSED.

